HST Office: install cleanly over the 1.0.0 betas 1-4 that were installed under LibreOffice's UpgradeCode.

Betas 1-4 stamped HST's executables 26.8.1.1; the new files carry their real version (1.0.0.x).
Costing skips every component whose key file on disk is newer, then RemoveExistingProducts
deletes the old copies, so those files were missing after an over-install.

- upgrade.pm: a detect-only twin of the legacy removal row (same code and range, attributes 258)
  sets HSTLEGACYPRODUCTS when such a beta is installed. It is a secure property, so it reaches
  the execute sequence of a full-UI install.
- HstLegacyReinstallMode / HstLegacyNoVcRedist (type 51), right after FindRelatedProducts in the
  execute and UI sequences and before any costing, run only when HSTLEGACYPRODUCTS is set:
  REINSTALLMODE=amus makes costing install the files whatever the version on disk, and
  VC_REDIST=0 leaves the C++ runtime merge-module components (condition VC_REDIST=1, permanent)
  out of costing, so the forced reinstall can never replace the runtime in System32; the betas
  installed it permanently, so it stays. A fresh install or an upgrade from beta.5 on sets
  neither. Everything runs in the execute sequence, so silent installs (/qn) and the updater
  (/passive) work the same.
- HstLegacyBeta: in an interactive install, a Vietnamese notice before the welcome page that the
  old test version will be removed and documents are not affected (Continue / Exit). The install
  never depends on it.

Side effects: in-use files of the old beta (the Explorer shell extension) are replaced too, so
msiexec returns 3010 (restart needed) more often. Fonts installed to the Fonts folder are
rewritten with the same files.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

